significant","donor_padj":0.985617,"donor_log2fc":0.0710262,"donor_lfcse":0.0950413,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":8.12454e-06}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000120370","entrez_id":["92344"],"uniprot":["Q5T7V8"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the golgin family, a group of coiled-coil proteins localized to the Golgi. The encoded protein may function in the secretory pathway. The encoded protein, which also localizes to the cytoplasm, was identified by interactions with the N-terminal kinase-like protein, and thus it may function in mitosis. Mutations in this gene have been associated with geroderma osteodysplastica. Alternatively spliced transcript variants have been described. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q5T7V8","text":"Plays a role in the organization and function of the Golgi apparatus. Involved in protein post-translational modification, particularly glycosylation of extracellular matrix proteins. Functions at the trans-Golgi by cooperating with SCYL1 to promote COPI coat assembly into discrete functional domains, supporting Golgi organization and trafficking."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}